<section class="w-full px-4 sm:px-8 pt-8 pb-16">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 mt-6 mb-4 max-[900px]:flex-col max-[900px]:items-start">
    <div>
      <p class="uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-xs text-primary font-semibold">
        Getting started
      </p>
      <h1 class="text-[clamp(2rem,4vw,3.4rem)] leading-[1.02]">
        Install to first finding in five minutes
      </h1>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.7]">
        ControlKeel turns project rules, domain knowledge, and security boundaries into findings, proofs, approval gates, budgets, evals, and durable context across supported hosts. Agent output is cheap; reviewability, release safety, and cost control are not. ControlKeel governs that loop from the first attach.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="w-full px-4 sm:px-8 pt-0 pb-16">
  <div class="space-y-4">
    <p class="uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-xs text-primary font-semibold">Install</p>
    <%= for channel <- @install_channels do %>
      <article
        class="rounded-3xl border bg-background/70 p-5 transition hover:border-primary/40 hover:bg-background/90"
        id={"install-channel-#{channel.id}"}
      >
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-start sm:justify-between">
          <div class="space-y-3">
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">{channel.label}</h3>
              <span class="rounded-full bg-muted px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-muted-foreground">
                {Enum.join(channel.platforms, ", ")}
              </span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-muted-foreground">{channel.description}</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border bg-overlay/10">
          <pre class="whitespace-pre-wrap px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-foreground"><code>{channel.command}</code></pre>
        </div>
      </article>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="w-full px-4 sm:px-8 pt-0 pb-16">
  <p class="uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-xs text-primary font-semibold">
    Quick start
  </p>
  <div class="border bg-card rounded-3xl backdrop-blur-[18px] shadow-[0_24px_80px_rgba(0,0,0,0.22)] p-6 mt-4">
    <p class="uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-xs text-primary font-semibold">
      Packaged binary
    </p>
    <ol class="grid gap-4 m-0 p-0 list-none mt-4">
      <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        1. Run <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">controlkeel</code>
        to boot the local web app.
      </li>
      <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        2. In your project, run <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">controlkeel setup</code>, then <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">controlkeel attach opencode</code>.
      </li>
      <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        3. Binding auto-bootstraps on first use; use
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">
          controlkeel bootstrap
        </code>
        or <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">controlkeel init</code>
        to do it explicitly.
      </li>
      <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        4. Run <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">controlkeel attach doctor</code>, <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">controlkeel provider doctor</code>, and <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">controlkeel status</code>.
      </li>
      <li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        5. Trigger a controlled validation, then open Session Control or run
        <code class="rounded bg-muted px-1.5 py-0.5 text-foreground">
          controlkeel findings
        </code>
        to verify the block.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground mt-4 text-sm">
    Attach defaults to project scope and writes inside the governed repository. User scope is available only for hosts that advertise it. Local stdio MCP exposes the full local tool set; hosted MCP is a separate, narrower OAuth-scoped surface.
  </p>
</section>

